From: nightcarnage
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] drm/amdgpu: fix golden GB_ADDR_CONFIG for gfx1013/gfx10

Change hardware golden register mmGB_ADDR_CONFIG from 0x00000044 to
0x00100044 for the gfx10 family. Bit 20 controls NUM_SHADER_ENGINES;
setting it from 0 to 2 fixes GPU address swizzle on BC-250.

The software path already uses CYAN_SKILLFISH_GB_ADDR_CONFIG_GOLDEN
(0x00100044) for IP_VERSION(10,1,3) and (10,1,4), but the hardware
golden register was still programming the stock value. The GPU memory
controller uses the hardware register value for physical address decode,
so the hardware and software must agree.

Credit: BC-250 community, documented by GabriWar.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c
index 1893cee..785f5ca 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gfx_v10_0.c
@@ -1641,7 +1641,7 @@ static const struct soc15_reg_golden golden_settings_gc_10_1_2[] = {
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmDB_DEBUG4, 0xffffffff, 0x04900000),
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmDB_DFSM_TILES_IN_FLIGHT, 0x0000ffff, 0x0000003f),
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmDB_LAST_OF_BURST_CONFIG, 0xffffffff, 0x03860204),
-	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmGB_ADDR_CONFIG, 0x0c1800ff, 0x00000044),
+	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmGB_ADDR_CONFIG, 0x0c1800ff, 0x00100044),
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmGCR_GENERAL_CNTL, 0x1ff0ffff, 0x00000500),
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmGE_PRIV_CONTROL, 0x00007fff, 0x000001fe),
 	SOC15_REG_GOLDEN_VALUE(GC, 0, mmGL1_PIPE_STEER, 0xffffffff, 0xe4e4e4e4),
